# What must never enter the image.
#
# The first two entries are not housekeeping — they are the licence and the
# secrets. Everything else is build hygiene.

# The licensed EmanuelleDev pack (ATTRIBUTION.md): redistribution is forbidden,
# and an image pushed to a registry is redistribution. The API server has no use
# for art in any case — Netlify serves the client.
assets/
apps/client/public/assets/

# Secrets live in App Runner's configuration, never in a layer. A .env copied
# into an image is readable by anyone who can pull it (CLAUDE.md §8).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Nothing here is server code.
#
# The manifests are the exception: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` verifies the
# lockfile against every workspace project it describes, so a missing
# package.json makes the install fail rather than skip. Only the manifests come
# in — none of the source.
apps/mapmaker
!apps/mapmaker/package.json
apps/client/src
apps/client/public
apps/client/*.html
docs
ROADMAP.md
README.md
*.md
!ATTRIBUTION.md

coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
